================================================================================
2. COMPONENTS THAT ARE *NOT* REDISTRIBUTED
================================================================================

These are used to build, register or test the engine. No part of them ships inside
the managed solution, so no attribution travels with this artifact. They are listed
only to make the boundary explicit.

  Microsoft.CrmSdk.CoreAssemblies (Microsoft.Xrm.Sdk, Microsoft.Crm.Sdk.Proxy)
    The engine compiles against these, but Dataverse supplies them at runtime. The
    solution's PluginAssemblies folder contains exactly one assembly - the engine's
    own AscentixRulesEnginePlugin.dll - and no Microsoft SDK assembly is
    packaged with it. Governed by the license accompanying that NuGet package.

  Build and test tooling, each under its own license: esbuild, TypeScript,
  vitest, jsdom, marked, @playwright/test, the @testing-library packages, the
  @types/* declaration packages, xunit, xunit.runner.visualstudio,
  Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk and FakeXrmEasy.9.

  tslib is present in the source tree's node_modules but is not reachable from any
  bundle entry point and is not present in any shipped web resource.

  marked converts this product's own Markdown documentation to HTML at build time;
  the resulting HTML is Ascentix content and no marked code is bundled.


================================================================================
3. HOW TO VERIFY
================================================================================

The set of components bundled into asx_ruleeditor.js is reproducible: build the
client with `npm run build` under client/ and pass esbuild `--metafile`; every
third-party input appears in the metafile. The Manrope embedding is produced by
client/scripts/build-font-css.mjs.
